WEBVTT

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.042
is a great example
of what you would call stress.

00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:02.217
(Laughs)

00:15:02.241 --> 00:15:03.402
AG: Yes.

00:15:03.426 --> 00:15:06.458
And I would just like to learn
to not even find that stressful.

00:15:06.482 --> 00:15:07.711
This my stance on it.

00:15:07.735 --> 00:15:10.478
As opposed to saying,
"I'm burned out, I can't do this."

00:15:10.502 --> 00:15:16.633
AHP: Right. So when, I'm frantically going
between my work and personal email

00:15:16.657 --> 00:15:19.817
trying to, like, respond
to all these things and, like, make lists

00:15:19.841 --> 00:15:22.746
and that sort of thing,
and like actually not doing anything,

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:26.506
I'm like, "This is a weird behavior
that you're doing."

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:31.469
Having realized that I'm burnt out,
I recognize burnout behaviors.